# Glance (deck + swaps)

Algorithms and plate geometry: [`docs/glance-layout.md`](../../docs/glance-layout.md). Prefer existing shared helpers before adding a parallel constant, converter, or pipeline.

## Share

- Plate / peek: `packages/shared/src/deck-builder/glance/plate.ts`
- Card conversion / fingerprint base: `card-from-instance.ts`, `card-identity.ts`
- API: `glance-pipeline.ts` (cache + miss path), `glance-art.ts` (placements/cards — no fake plan adapters)
- Render faces/badges via shared helpers; product chrome in `glance-render-deck` / `glance-render-swap`
- Web: `glance-http.ts`, `glance-png.ts`, `glance-ui.tsx`

## Keep separate

- Deck L-masonry (`glance/layout.ts`) vs swap densify / pack / masonry / planner
- Product packing gaps and margins (do not equalize for consistency)
- Product dialogs and option UIs
- Deck vs swap unit/API/web test suites (file-local builders OK; grow `tests/api/helpers/glance-render.ts`)

## Generation versions

Bump `GLANCE_GENERATION_VERSION` / `SWAP_GLANCE_GENERATION_VERSION` when fingerprints, colours, art tier, pixels, or delivery change. Do **not** bump for pure moves or identical-math extracts.

## Avoid

- Merging deck and swap planners, plan types, or whole dialogs
- Casting one product’s plan into the other for art/prefetch
- Cross-layer “glance test kit” or soft dual-outcome API cases that hide bugs
